<title>UK: Mexico sets $1.0 billion five-year FRN.</title>
<headline>Mexico sets $1.0 billion five-year FRN.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following floating-rate issue was announced by joint lead managers HSBC Markets and Merrill Lynch.</p>
<p> BORROWER   MEXICO</p>
<p> AMT    $1.0 BLN	BASE	 3M-LIBOR  MATURITY    *  JUN.02</p>
<p> TYPE	 FRN	 MARGIN     +125 BP   PAY DATE    27.JUN.97</p>
<p> LAST MOODY BA2	 ISS PRICE  **	  FULL FEES   0.375</p>
<p> LAST S&amp;P   BB	  REOFFER    **</p>
<p> NOTES   ** TO BE PRICED TO YIELD 3ML +140 BP</p>
<p>	    * CALL AT PAR FROM JUNE 2000</p>
<p> LISTING    LUX	 DENOMS (K) 10+1   SALE LIMITS</p>
<p>US/UK/MX/JP/HK</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    NEW YORK  HOME CTRY  MEXICO    TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.125     SELL CONC  0.25	PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p> NOTES	PRICING DUE ON JUNE 20</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8863</p>
